WEBVTT

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:10.560
Hey, over here! Throw it here!

00:00:10.770 --> 00:00:11.860
S-Stop!

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:13.060
Here it goes!

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:16.070
Give it back! Please!

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:17.400
Over here!

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:20.740
You're so irritating to look at!
Always scared of something!

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:23.740
Come get it if you want it back!

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:35.250
A dream...

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:41.260
I'd rather be alone than risk
getting hurt by someone...

00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:45.600
That's how I protected myself...

00:00:46.970 --> 00:00:49.310
...since I was very little.

00:02:23.110 --> 00:02:25.910
That was such a long time ago...

00:02:26.530 --> 00:02:28.200
...and I'm not in grade school anymore.

00:02:36.580 --> 00:02:37.500
This way!

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:39.290
Wait up! Wait!

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:43.590
Something's wrong!

00:02:44.590 --> 00:02:47.010
Someone...

00:02:53.710 --> 00:02:57.100
Um... are you okay?

00:03:07.030 --> 00:03:07.950
Um...

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:08.610
Look.

00:03:09.780 --> 00:03:11.950
Look... under the eaves?

00:03:12.370 --> 00:03:13.370
Yes.

00:03:17.710 --> 00:03:21.000
That's my cat. She won't come out...

00:03:22.290 --> 00:03:28.380
We're on our way to the vet,
but she really hates the hospital...

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:31.910
Come on, Sakura, come out!

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:32.850
I know!

00:03:33.140 --> 00:03:35.730
Can you wait one moment?

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:46.860
You must be scared. I understand.

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:50.570
But it's okay. You can come out.

00:03:52.950 --> 00:03:54.160
Gotcha!

00:03:57.790 --> 00:04:00.670
Thank you so much! You saved me.

00:04:00.830 --> 00:04:02.130
Please, it's nothing...

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:05.670
Are you some sort of cat master?

00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:07.830
Huh...? Cat master...?

00:04:07.830 --> 00:04:14.500
She's so shy and usually never lets
anyone other than me touch her.

00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:17.000
Not even my little sister.

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:18.370
Really?

00:04:18.370 --> 00:04:23.210
Earlier she ran under there because
she got startled by the kids' voices.

00:04:23.210 --> 00:04:26.870
Oh... those kids.

00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:31.040
Shy... Is that what we have in common?

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:31.870
Hmm?

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:34.080
Oh, it's nothing...

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:35.330
But...

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:36.660
But?

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:43.870
I, um... I do understand how it could be scary
to approach someone you don't know.

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:46.830
What about me?

00:04:46.830 --> 00:04:48.410
Do I scare you, too?

00:04:48.410 --> 00:04:52.830
N-Not at all! You actually make me feel safe...

00:04:52.830 --> 00:04:57.960
Good! You do have some
things in common with Sakura.

00:04:57.960 --> 00:05:00.290
Do you think so...?

00:05:00.290 --> 00:05:02.910
I don't know if we're that similar, but...

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:07.460
Cats are warm... She makes me feel happy.

00:05:07.460 --> 00:05:11.290
Oh, we have to get to the hospital now.

00:05:11.290 --> 00:05:13.290
Oh, me, too...

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:15.290
Are you going somewhere today?

00:05:15.290 --> 00:05:18.160
Yes, I'm scheduled to meet some friends.

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:20.370
Oh, sorry I kept you.

00:05:20.370 --> 00:05:25.960
No, it was great to talk to you.
Thank you for the tea!

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:28.660
Thanks again!

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:37.000
Oh, there she is! Hey, Miki-chan!

00:05:38.210 --> 00:05:39.620
Did something happen, Miki?

00:05:39.620 --> 00:05:42.250
Sorry to make you wait...

00:05:42.250 --> 00:05:44.500
Is everything okay?

00:05:44.500 --> 00:05:46.830
Um, well...

00:05:46.830 --> 00:05:49.410
Come on, we can talk later.

00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:52.410
For now let's go to my house!

00:05:52.410 --> 00:05:54.040
Sure, sure.

00:05:55.160 --> 00:05:59.120
It's been so long since the last time
I visited a friend's house...

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:00.620
I'm a bit tense.

00:06:04.210 --> 00:06:06.830
I see, so that's what happened.

00:06:06.830 --> 00:06:09.500
Yeah, and that's why I was late...

00:06:09.500 --> 00:06:13.050
Good job, Miki-chan!
Don't worry about it, you helped someone.

00:06:13.050 --> 00:06:17.260
Yeah, compared to Aya,
who just overslept and came late.

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:23.750
I didn't know cats could be so stubborn,
not responding to their owner.

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:26.290
Cats can be really timid.

00:06:26.290 --> 00:06:28.080
Timid...

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:29.370
What's wrong, Miki?

00:06:29.370 --> 00:06:31.870
Oh... it's nothing.

00:06:31.870 --> 00:06:36.000
My cat won't let me touch her either!

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:37.040
Your cat?

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:38.040
Yeah.

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:41.040
Anyway, I wonder where my sister is.

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:43.750
I want to play games with four players!

00:06:44.910 --> 00:06:47.120
Oh, she's finally back!

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:51.080
A cat...?

00:06:51.080 --> 00:06:55.210
That's our cat, Sakura. Sakura!

00:06:57.120 --> 00:06:59.330
Always so cold.

00:06:59.330 --> 00:07:01.620
Oh... so...

00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:04.080
Hey, Aya, I'm home.

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:06.460
Hey! I brought friends.

00:07:06.460 --> 00:07:08.660
Oh, aren't you...?

00:07:20.070 --> 00:07:24.910
It's quite a miracle how
Miki-chan met Hana, isn't it?

00:07:25.160 --> 00:07:29.000
I was surprised. Thanks again for the help.

00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:32.500
Let me reintroduce myself.
I'm Takayashiki Hana, Aya's elder sister.

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:33.750
Nice to meet you.

00:07:34.840 --> 00:07:39.590
I'm Takekasa Miki. Nice to meet you, too.

00:07:39.590 --> 00:07:42.280
I'm so glad to see you again, Miki-chan.

00:07:42.280 --> 00:07:43.810
Me, too...!

00:07:44.220 --> 00:07:48.560
Is she really your sister? She's super pretty!

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:49.790
What does that mean...?

00:07:50.310 --> 00:07:51.270
And you are...?

00:07:51.770 --> 00:07:55.780
Nice to meet you.
I'm Ono Midori, Aya-san's classmate.

00:07:55.780 --> 00:07:58.790
Thank you for inviting us
to your house today.

00:07:58.790 --> 00:08:02.790
Oh, how polite.
Nice to meet you, too, Midori-chan.

00:08:02.790 --> 00:08:04.960
Yes, thank you!

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:08.460
And this is my best friend...

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:10.330
I'm Maki! Nice to meet ya.

00:08:10.330 --> 00:08:13.960
I thought, the more the merrier,
so I had her come over.

00:08:13.960 --> 00:08:16.370
I-I see.

00:08:16.370 --> 00:08:19.460
She has some interesting friends.

00:08:19.460 --> 00:08:21.330
Yeah...

00:08:21.330 --> 00:08:24.080
Oh, no...

00:08:24.080 --> 00:08:26.540
She's not the type I'm comfortable around...

00:08:26.540 --> 00:08:29.580
I'm Aya! Nice to meet you, Maki-chan!

00:08:29.580 --> 00:08:33.290
So you're Hana's sister, huh?

00:08:33.290 --> 00:08:37.210
I can tell. You're not scared of me one bit.

00:08:37.210 --> 00:08:42.540
Hana helps me out with stuff all the time.
Let me know if you need a hand!

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:43.500
Okay!

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:46.460
Um, where did you two meet...?

00:08:46.460 --> 00:08:49.160
I met her at work!

00:08:49.160 --> 00:08:53.410
There was a drunk customer
harassing me and she saved me.

00:08:53.410 --> 00:08:55.960
It was super awesome!

00:08:55.960 --> 00:09:01.160
You have to keep an eye on Hana.
There's always a creep trying to get near her!

00:09:01.160 --> 00:09:03.790
They run away when I'm with Maki-chan.

00:09:03.790 --> 00:09:05.580
That's right, I totally--

00:09:05.580 --> 00:09:07.250
Hey, Hana!

00:09:08.410 --> 00:09:09.910
Jeez...

00:09:12.910 --> 00:09:15.790
I guess she could be a nice person after all...?

00:09:17.080 --> 00:09:19.580
I wonder if Sakura will come out.

00:09:19.580 --> 00:09:22.290
Come here, Sakura-chan!

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:24.960
Oh. Guess not.

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:29.370
It's not just you.
She won't even let me touch her.

00:09:29.370 --> 00:09:32.370
She didn't have a problem with
Miki though, and it was her first time.

00:09:32.370 --> 00:09:34.830
Midori-chan, you're mean!

00:09:34.830 --> 00:09:39.500
But seriously, she was on
Miki-chan 's lap and purring.

00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:42.620
Miki-chan, what kind of
technique did you pull off?!

00:09:42.620 --> 00:09:44.620
Huh? Technique?

00:09:44.620 --> 00:09:46.910
She's a cat master.

00:09:46.910 --> 00:09:52.290
Hey, have I seen you before somewhere?

00:09:52.290 --> 00:09:55.500
Miki-chan, was it?
Which middle school did you go to?

00:09:55.500 --> 00:09:58.710
Um... Kamogawa-West.

00:09:58.710 --> 00:10:02.580
Seriously?! Same as me!
I'm from Kamo-West, too!

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:07.000
So you're a <i>kouhai</i>, huh?
Then I guess I must have seen you at school.

00:10:08.410 --> 00:10:12.080
But they're still first-year
high school students.

00:10:12.080 --> 00:10:14.210
You couldn't have gone
to school at the same time.

00:10:14.210 --> 00:10:18.830
What? Hmm... then where...?

00:10:18.830 --> 00:10:22.910
I know I've met her before somewhere...

00:10:22.910 --> 00:10:26.080
A long time ago... somewhere...

00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:27.620
Oh, well!

00:10:27.620 --> 00:10:30.370
Anyway, wanna get on it?

00:10:30.370 --> 00:10:32.870
Maki-chan is good at games, too.

00:10:32.870 --> 00:10:35.330
That's right!
I'm unbeatable at fighting games!

00:10:35.330 --> 00:10:36.160
Fighting...?

00:10:36.160 --> 00:10:37.580
Fighting video games!

00:10:37.580 --> 00:10:40.940
No, Maki-chan,
we're playing board games today.

00:10:41.540 --> 00:10:42.790
Board games...?

00:10:42.790 --> 00:10:44.290
Midori-chan, you're up!

00:10:44.290 --> 00:10:50.080
Yes, yes. To be exact, since there's
no board, it's not a "board game," but...

00:10:50.960 --> 00:10:54.250
<i>Incan Gold? </i>What's this?

00:10:54.250 --> 00:10:56.210
It's a game from overseas.

00:10:56.210 --> 00:11:00.580
Lately Aya's been raving on and on
about how much fun board games are,

00:11:00.580 --> 00:11:02.500
so I got interested.

00:11:02.500 --> 00:11:06.000
This is a game...? Never seen this before.

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:10.160
You're behind the times, Maki-chan!
They make tons of them in Germany!

00:11:10.160 --> 00:11:14.040
Really now, Aya-chan? Well then, can
you describe what kind of game this is?

00:11:14.040 --> 00:11:18.580
Well, this is... Tell her, Midori-chan!

00:11:18.580 --> 00:11:19.870
Yes, yes.

00:11:20.870 --> 00:11:26.580
In this game, <i>Incan Gold</i>, players
become explorers who explore a ruin.

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:30.660
The player to bring back
the most jewels wins.

00:11:30.660 --> 00:11:35.540
The rules are simple. First, flip
the top card of the deck faceup.

00:11:35.540 --> 00:11:37.790
If you get one of these treasure cards,

00:11:37.790 --> 00:11:42.910
it means you found the
number of jewels on the card.

00:11:42.910 --> 00:11:45.250
In this case, 11.

00:11:45.250 --> 00:11:49.210
The jewels found are split
evenly amongst all of the players.

00:11:49.210 --> 00:11:53.410
In this case, there are five
of us, so we each get two.

00:11:53.410 --> 00:11:58.540
The remainder, one jewel,
is left on this card.

00:11:58.540 --> 00:12:01.710
I see. So we collect these.

00:12:01.710 --> 00:12:07.750
We continue on, flipping cards
and getting jewels, but...

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:10.080
Snakes?!

00:12:10.080 --> 00:12:12.290
This is a hazard card.

00:12:12.290 --> 00:12:18.250
Half of the 30-card deck, 15 cards,
are actually these hazard cards.

00:12:18.250 --> 00:12:20.080
Half?!

00:12:20.080 --> 00:12:21.750
And if you draw that card...?

00:12:21.750 --> 00:12:26.410
The first card is a "premonition,"
so nothing happens. But...

00:12:26.410 --> 00:12:31.620
...if a second copy of the same type
of hazard appears, the exploration fails.

00:12:31.620 --> 00:12:35.750
The explorers must escape from the ruins.

00:12:35.750 --> 00:12:41.660
When that happens, you lose all
of the treasure that you found.

00:12:41.660 --> 00:12:42.750
What?!

00:12:42.750 --> 00:12:43.830
Oh.

00:12:43.830 --> 00:12:45.210
Hm.

00:12:45.210 --> 00:12:51.960
The types of hazards are snakes, spiders,
mummies, flame trap, and falling rocks.

00:12:51.960 --> 00:12:56.660
There are three copies of these
five types, totaling 15 cards.

00:12:56.660 --> 00:13:01.290
In order to keep the jewels that you found,
you must decide after every card

00:13:01.290 --> 00:13:04.830
whether you want to continue on,
or go home early.

00:13:04.830 --> 00:13:07.620
Decide? You mean, just say out loud?

00:13:07.620 --> 00:13:11.210
No, you use this explorer token for that.

00:13:11.210 --> 00:13:14.290
If you want to go home,
hold the token in your hand.

00:13:14.290 --> 00:13:20.540
To keep going, keep your hand empty.
Then, everyone reveals it at the same time.

00:13:23.210 --> 00:13:26.330
I see. I get it, glasses girl!

00:13:26.330 --> 00:13:32.000
You can take the risk for more treasure,
or get scared and run for your life...

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:33.870
In essence, this game is...

00:13:33.870 --> 00:13:35.710
...a chicken race!

00:13:36.960 --> 00:13:40.370
That's correct, this is a chicken race.

00:13:40.370 --> 00:13:44.330
The further you go, the more dangerous it gets,

00:13:44.330 --> 00:13:49.410
but with fewer explorers remaining,
your share of the jewels increases.

00:13:49.410 --> 00:13:52.330
When you decide to go back,
you just have to be careful.

00:13:52.330 --> 00:13:53.410
Hmm?

00:13:53.410 --> 00:13:59.250
That's because the jewels you
found aren't yours at that point.

00:13:59.250 --> 00:14:00.620
What does that mean?

00:14:00.620 --> 00:14:05.080
Only by going back do you
get proper ownership of the jewels,

00:14:05.080 --> 00:14:09.000
allowing you to put them in
your tent as your earnings.

00:14:09.000 --> 00:14:13.960
I see. There's still a possibility
that you'd lose the jewels you found.

00:14:13.960 --> 00:14:20.660
Right. So in order to get points to win
the game, you must go home or keep winning.

00:14:20.660 --> 00:14:22.410
I see.

00:14:23.460 --> 00:14:28.500
Also, when you go home, you get
to take the jewels you left on the cards.

00:14:28.500 --> 00:14:31.000
Oh, the person who goes
home gets to keep those!

00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:38.120
One game consists of five rounds.
The person to gather the most points wins.

00:14:38.120 --> 00:14:40.160
By the way, there are three types of jewels.

00:14:40.620 --> 00:14:44.910
Blue is turquoise, the cheapest one,
which is only worth one dollar.

00:14:44.910 --> 00:14:48.870
Obsidian is worth five dollars
and gold is worth ten dollars.

00:14:48.870 --> 00:14:51.620
Do you understand the rules?

00:14:51.620 --> 00:14:53.500
Yes...

00:14:53.500 --> 00:14:54.960
Mostly, I guess...

00:14:54.960 --> 00:14:57.240
What? Are you unsure, Hana?

00:14:57.460 --> 00:15:00.870
Well, Hana can pair up with Maki-chan.

00:15:00.870 --> 00:15:04.750
Oh, is that allowed?
Maki-chan, would that be okay?

00:15:04.750 --> 00:15:07.870
Sure, why not? Anyway...

00:15:07.870 --> 00:15:10.580
...a chicken race, eh?

00:15:10.580 --> 00:15:13.250
Time to get that blood boiling again...

00:15:14.290 --> 00:15:16.500
Um, what do you mean...?

00:15:16.970 --> 00:15:21.970
{Between}

00:15:23.330 --> 00:15:27.830
Hmm... one more mummy or flame
and we'll be in trouble...

00:15:27.830 --> 00:15:31.250
Moving on! Let's go!

00:15:31.250 --> 00:15:33.290
So Miki's the only one who's going back.

00:15:33.290 --> 00:15:35.660
What? Already?

00:15:35.660 --> 00:15:37.750
Yes... sorry...

00:15:37.750 --> 00:15:40.830
Don't get too greedy,
you'll get another mummy.

00:15:40.830 --> 00:15:43.750
Don't worry! Go, go, go!

00:15:43.750 --> 00:15:47.790
So there's three of us left.
Flipping the next card...

00:15:47.790 --> 00:15:50.620
Yeah! Five dollar obsidian, here we go!

00:15:50.620 --> 00:15:54.410
See? It's a lot harder to die than you'd think.

00:15:57.120 --> 00:16:01.430
Hey, Miki-chan.
You used to be bullied a lot, right?

00:16:01.870 --> 00:16:10.330
I can tell. Bullies have an instinct--they can
sense people who are weaker than them.

00:16:10.330 --> 00:16:15.000
With that attitude of yours,
you're practically asking to get bullied.

00:16:16.080 --> 00:16:20.120
You're so irritating to look at!
Always scared of something!

00:16:20.120 --> 00:16:23.330
I think... there was one girl in that group

00:16:23.330 --> 00:16:26.620
I didn't know the name of
who was older than the others...

00:16:27.710 --> 00:16:29.620
Could it be...?!

00:16:29.620 --> 00:16:30.710
Maki-chan!

00:16:31.750 --> 00:16:35.090
I won't allow anyone to bully Miki-chan!

00:16:35.090 --> 00:16:36.160
She's right!

00:16:37.160 --> 00:16:39.170
I will protect Miki!

00:16:39.880 --> 00:16:42.910
Midori-chan... Aya-chan...

00:16:42.910 --> 00:16:45.620
Oh, what good friendships.

00:16:45.620 --> 00:16:48.460
Let's see if you have
the courage to match it!

00:16:48.460 --> 00:16:50.580
Let's go!

00:16:50.580 --> 00:16:52.540
Huh?

00:16:52.540 --> 00:16:54.000
See ya!

00:16:54.000 --> 00:16:59.000
Oh, so you're leaving, Maki-chan?
You're not as brave as we thought.

00:16:59.000 --> 00:17:00.280
Right, Midori-chan?

00:17:00.410 --> 00:17:05.660
Y-Yes. The two of us can split
all of the riches from here on!

00:17:05.660 --> 00:17:07.750
Open!

00:17:07.750 --> 00:17:11.080
No! The second mummy card!

00:17:12.210 --> 00:17:15.960
Got you both! I guess we win this round!

00:17:15.960 --> 00:17:17.710
That's great, Maki-chan!

00:17:17.710 --> 00:17:22.180
It's experience! I've never
lost these types of game before!

00:17:23.330 --> 00:17:27.790
Aya-chan... Midori-chan...
Hold it together...

00:17:27.790 --> 00:17:30.120
I'll beat you next time!

00:17:37.250 --> 00:17:39.790
All right! We're close to the finish line!

00:17:39.790 --> 00:17:42.500
I'll finish far ahead of you all as number one!

00:17:44.210 --> 00:17:46.960
I'll drop out here.

00:17:46.960 --> 00:17:50.120
What?! Giant spiders?!

00:17:50.120 --> 00:17:53.960
That's four types! Too many hazards!

00:17:53.960 --> 00:17:57.080
No whining, make your call! Let's go!

00:17:58.500 --> 00:18:00.750
Aya-chan, dropping out here, too, huh?

00:18:01.830 --> 00:18:03.040
I can't do it!

00:18:03.040 --> 00:18:05.500
So the only ones left are, me and...

00:18:05.500 --> 00:18:07.750
M-Me...

00:18:07.750 --> 00:18:10.750
Well, now, didn't expect you to be here.

00:18:10.750 --> 00:18:12.250
Not going home yet?

00:18:12.250 --> 00:18:14.000
That's... um...

00:18:14.000 --> 00:18:18.660
I never thought I'd go head to head with you.

00:18:18.660 --> 00:18:22.120
Head to head with her...

00:18:22.120 --> 00:18:24.000
Miki...

00:18:24.000 --> 00:18:26.960
Here we go. Open!

00:18:26.960 --> 00:18:28.460
Falling rocks!

00:18:28.460 --> 00:18:31.790
Now all five types of hazard cards are open!

00:18:31.790 --> 00:18:34.370
From here on, any hazard card means death!

00:18:34.370 --> 00:18:36.120
Miki-chan!

00:18:36.120 --> 00:18:39.660
If you fail here, you'll finish dead last.

00:18:39.660 --> 00:18:41.460
Now is a good time to pull out.

00:18:42.370 --> 00:18:47.080
If you pull out now, you won't be able
to beat me, but you'd still be second place.

00:18:47.080 --> 00:18:49.000
That's not bad, is it?

00:18:49.000 --> 00:18:50.210
I know...

00:18:50.210 --> 00:18:52.790
Besides, everyone knows I'm a coward.

00:18:52.790 --> 00:18:56.040
Even if I left now, nobody
would think less of me...

00:18:57.040 --> 00:18:59.710
Huh...? Warmth...?

00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:05.080
Sakura, have you come to cheer me up...?

00:19:06.410 --> 00:19:07.960
Miki...

00:19:12.620 --> 00:19:13.660
Miki-chan.

00:19:14.830 --> 00:19:17.120
Are you ready? Here it comes.

00:19:20.160 --> 00:19:22.620
Let's go!

00:19:22.620 --> 00:19:23.410
What?!

00:19:23.410 --> 00:19:24.290
Miki!

00:19:24.290 --> 00:19:25.550
Miki-chan?!

00:19:25.660 --> 00:19:30.540
Huh, surprising. But it's totally crazy!

00:19:30.540 --> 00:19:32.250
That's just suicide.

00:19:32.250 --> 00:19:38.000
This is my courage...
that I got from everyone's kindness...!

00:19:38.000 --> 00:19:41.660
If any hazard card comes out, it's over...

00:19:41.660 --> 00:19:44.960
Oh... it hurts to even watch...!

00:19:44.960 --> 00:19:46.160
Miki-chan...

00:19:53.000 --> 00:19:54.830
Jewels!

00:19:56.710 --> 00:19:58.710
Awesome, Miki-chan!

00:19:56.750 --> 00:19:58.330
Great!

00:19:58.870 --> 00:20:00.210
I did it!

00:20:00.210 --> 00:20:03.540
Miki, that's 15 jewels for you alone!

00:20:04.540 --> 00:20:05.750
Alone...

00:20:06.660 --> 00:20:08.750
You did it! You did it!

00:20:07.330 --> 00:20:08.130
No...

00:20:08.750 --> 00:20:10.510
Miki! You're awesome!

00:20:09.050 --> 00:20:11.430
No.

00:20:12.330 --> 00:20:17.370
I was able to move ahead
because I wasn't alone.

00:20:17.370 --> 00:20:20.710
Wow! Huge upset!

00:20:20.710 --> 00:20:24.790
Who would've imagined, me,
Maki Kyoko, losing in a game of courage?!

00:20:24.790 --> 00:20:28.910
Hey, you got me. I'm sorry
for saying those things earlier.

00:20:28.910 --> 00:20:29.750
Forgive me!

00:20:29.750 --> 00:20:33.620
Oh, no, please, don't do that...

00:20:33.620 --> 00:20:37.790
Kyoko...? Is your first
name Kyoko, Maki-san?

00:20:38.040 --> 00:20:39.830
Yeah, Maki is my last name.

00:20:39.830 --> 00:20:43.790
But call me Maki-chan!
I don't like my first name, Kyoko.

00:20:43.960 --> 00:20:46.540
Why? It's such a nice name!

00:20:46.540 --> 00:20:48.010
Maki... Kyoko...

00:20:49.260 --> 00:20:51.510
Kyoko... Kyoko...

00:20:53.290 --> 00:20:54.050
Kyoko!

00:20:54.510 --> 00:20:56.470
Ebisu

00:20:54.510 --> 00:20:56.470
Shrine

00:20:56.810 --> 00:20:59.310
Give it back! Please...

00:20:59.460 --> 00:21:00.410
Here it goes!

00:21:00.410 --> 00:21:01.600
Hey, hey!

00:21:01.310 --> 00:21:02.730
Over here!

00:21:03.410 --> 00:21:04.410
Huh...?

00:21:04.410 --> 00:21:07.040
What... What are you doing?! Oh...

00:21:08.210 --> 00:21:13.080
You're in middle school now,
but still picking on little girls?

00:21:13.080 --> 00:21:14.830
That's shameful.

00:21:14.830 --> 00:21:16.370
K-Kyoko!

00:21:16.370 --> 00:21:18.330
It's Mad Dog Kyoko!

00:21:18.330 --> 00:21:21.250
Get out of my face, losers!

00:21:31.540 --> 00:21:34.790
Mad Dog Kyoko...

00:21:34.790 --> 00:21:38.540
Wait, Miki-chan, how do
you know my old nickname?!

00:21:43.580 --> 00:21:46.830
Did we meet somewhere...?

00:21:48.870 --> 00:21:50.620
Yes.

00:21:50.620 --> 00:21:54.330
Where, though? I don't remember at all...

00:21:51.360 --> 00:21:57.450
Painful memories are like caves.
It's dark and scary and I couldn't get near it.

00:21:54.330 --> 00:21:57.450
Hey, Maki-chan, how did you
get to be called Mad Dog?

00:21:58.660 --> 00:22:01.330
But if I find the courage to push forward,

00:22:01.870 --> 00:22:05.540
sometimes, I can find precious
memories, like jewels in my past.

00:23:37.800 --> 00:23:39.930
Facing off against the student
council vice-chair in a game.

00:23:40.260 --> 00:23:43.010
If you lose, you have to give up on me.

00:23:43.770 --> 00:23:46.310
I have a dream I want to fulfill.
